all damage figures are against 400 defence unless stated
buffs saturate towards 3000 per mille of a stat's ceiling and debuffs towards 100 per mille of the stat,
so neither limit is ever reached and each further term is worth less than the last

== attack buffs ==
620 base attack, ceiling 800 so the limit it approaches is 2400
terms                              raw   actual   absorbed   damage    gain
none                             620      620          0      478   1.00x
+30%                             806      788         18      607   1.26x
+50%                             930      884         46      681   1.42x
+50% twice                      1240     1079        161      832   1.74x
+50% four times                 1860     1350        510     1041   2.17x
+50% eight times                3100     1656       1444     1277   2.67x
+120 flat                        740      732          8      564   1.17x
+120 flat then +50%             1110     1004        106      774   1.61x

== defence debuffs ==
800 attack against 560 defence, which cannot be driven below 56
terms                              raw   actual   damage    gain
none                             560      560      502   1.00x
-30%                             392      434      588   1.17x
-30% twice                       224      359      655   1.30x
-30% four times                 -112      272      755   1.50x
-100%                              0      295      726   1.44x
-300%                          -1120      173      913   1.81x
a term past -100% is safe to author, because it saturates instead of inverting

== elemental effectiveness ==
the term scales how far a matchup deviates from neutral, clamped to +1000 per mille
so it is worth more the worse the defender's matchup already is
term       matchup           multiplier   shifted   damage   shifted   gain
+30%       weak twice               2250      2625     1388      1620  1.16x
+30%       weak                     1500      1650      925      1018  1.10x
+30%       neutral                  1000      1000      617       617  1.00x
+30%       resisted                  667       667      411       411  1.00x
+100%      weak twice               2250      3500     1388      2160  1.55x
+100%      weak                     1500      2000      925      1234  1.33x
-100%      weak twice               2250      1000     1388       617  0.44x
-100%      weak                     1500      1000      925       617  0.66x

== accuracy ==
a skill's own accuracy is the floor and a certain hit is the limit it never reaches,
so the accuracy stat, ceiling 300, closes the gap with diminishing returns
skill accuracy        0      60     120     180     240     300   <- accuracy stat
           600      600     652     692     724     750     771
           700      700     750     785     812     833     850
           800      800     846     875     894     909     920
           850      850     892     916     931     942     950
           900      900     937     954     964     970     975
           950      950     977     985     989     991     992
          1000     1000    1000    1000    1000    1000    1000

an accuracy stat of a thousand times the ceiling still falls short of certainty
  a 700 skill with 300000 accuracy lands 999 per mille of the time
  a 900 skill with 300000 accuracy lands 999 per mille of the time
  a 1000 skill cannot miss at any accuracy, which is how a guaranteed effect is written

rolled over 100000 attempts, 800 attack, 1800 per mille
shape                   chance   landed   expected   measured
single strike               916      617        565        565
two strikes                 916      616        564        563
three strikes               916      615        563        563
splitting a skill into strikes leaves the expected damage alone and cuts the variance,
because every strike rolls on its own

== dodge ==
dodge reopens the gap accuracy closed, towards a floor of 150 it never reaches
it is applied after accuracy rather than subtracted from it, so it bites even against
an attack that was going to land almost every time
chance before dodge       0     30     60     90    120    150   <- dodge stat
                600     600    572    548    525    506    488
                700     700    672    646    623    602    583
                850     850    822    795    771    748    727
                950     950    922    895    870    846    824
                992     992    964    936    911    887    865
                999     999    971    943    918    894    872

what each stat is worth against an 850 per mille skill
stat        points   chance   change   per point
none              0      850        0        0.00
accuracy        300      950      100        0.33
dodge           150      727     -123        0.82
the dodge ceiling is 150 against accuracy's 300, which is what pays for dodge working
against a wider gap and therefore being worth more per point

a guaranteed skill ignores dodge entirely, which is what leaves block a job to do
  a 1000 skill against      0 dodge lands 1000 per mille of the time
  a 1000 skill against    150 dodge lands 1000 per mille of the time
  a 1000 skill against 300000 dodge lands 1000 per mille of the time

== block charges ==
a charge cancels one strike that would otherwise have landed, guaranteed hits included,
and is only spent on a strike that connects, so dodging wastes none
a guaranteed skill splitting 1800 per mille of power, against one charge, 800 attack
shape            per strike   blocked   struck    dealt   share stopped
 1 x 1800                617         1        0        0         100.0%
 2 x 900                 308         1        1      308          50.0%
 3 x 600                 205         1        2      410          33.3%
 5 x 360                 123         1        4      492          20.0%
 6 x 300                 102         1        5      510          16.6%
one charge erases a single heavy blow and is burned by a sixth of one,
so multi strike is the answer to block just as block is the answer to a heavy hit

several charges at once, capped at 3, against a guaranteed 3 x 600 skill
charges   blocked   struck    dealt   share stopped   prevented per charge
      0         0        3      615           0.0%                      0
      1         1        2      410          33.3%                    205
      2         2        1      205          66.6%                    205
      3         3        0        0         100.0%                    205
      4         3        0        0         100.0%                    205
every charge is worth exactly as much as the first: charges are the one defence
in the engine that does not saturate, which is why they are capped instead

what a full stack of 3 charges is worth against single heavy hits
incoming attacks   dealt without charges   dealt with them   share stopped
               1                     617                 0         100.0%
               2                    1234                 0         100.0%
               3                    1851                 0         100.0%
               4                    2468               617          75.0%
               5                    3085              1234          60.0%
a full stack negates a whole round of heavy single hits, so it belongs on a long
cooldown; against chip damage the same stack is worth almost nothing

the counter triangle
  attacker choice        beaten by        beats
  normal accuracy        dodge            block, which it wastes on misses
  guaranteed hit         block            dodge, which it ignores
  multi strike           nothing directly dodge by averaging, block by burning charges
  single heavy hit       block, dodge     armour, since one big number beats the defence curve

