== damage over time, poison at 500 per mille per stack per tick ==
3 stacks at most, 3 turns each, refreshed on every application
ticks go through the defence curve like any other damage and are never rolled,
so a status cannot be dodged or blocked once it has landed

the ramp against 400 defence, one stack applied per turn for three turns
victim turn   stacks   tick   cumulative   as direct hits
          1        1    171          171            0.27x
          2        2    342          513            0.83x
          3        3    513         1026            1.66x
          4        3    513         1539            2.49x
          5        3    513         2052            3.32x
          6        0      0         2052            3.32x
          7        0      0         2052            3.32x

the three turns spent applying could have been three direct hits for 1851,
so the poison is worth 1.10x of the damage it gave up, in exchange for
ignoring dodge and block and for setting up a skill that needs a status

the same ramp against each profile, showing the defence curve still applies
profile                  def   tick at 3 stacks   total   three direct hits    ratio
bulwark, max health      400                513    2052                1851    1.10x
sentinel, max defence    800                327    1308                1176    1.11x
vanguard, balanced       560                417    1668                1506    1.10x
duelist, max attack      320                579    2316                2088    1.10x
skirmisher, max speed    250                654    2616                2355    1.11x

when a cleanse lands, and what it saves
cleanse on turn   damage through   saved   share saved
              1             1197     855         41.6%
              2              684    1368         66.6%
              3              513    1539         75.0%
              4             1026    1026         50.0%
              5             1539     513         25.0%
              6             2052       0          0.0%
          never             2052       0          0.0%
the cheapest turn to cleanse is the attacker's last application, not the first:
cleanse earlier and the stack is simply rebuilt, cleanse later and the ticks are
already paid, so the defender has to read when the attacker stops

what a detonate gives up, by the stack count it consumes
stacks consumed   remaining ticks lost   a burst matching it needs power
              1                    513                             1496
              2                   1026                             2992
              3                   1539                             4488
a detonate priced at that power is exactly break even, so it should sit below it
and be paid for by arriving now instead of over three turns

total damage does not depend on speed, because duration counts the victim's turns
turns simulated   total
              3     513
             10     513
             40     513
a hasted victim takes its ticks sooner, not more often

